      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm not saying it's a massive government conspiracy, but just think about how much these companies spend on R&D. they already use neuro-marketing to change how we perceive colors and shapes. if they can fine-tune a scent to make a bakery smell better, how hard would it be to actually fine-tune a scent to trigger a physical hunger response? like, doesn't it make sense that they would find ways to bypass our willpower if it increases their profit margins? it feels like there's a point where \"marketing\" just becomes \"biological manipulation.\"",
